"**too … to / enough … to / so … as to / in order to / so as to:** *He is **too weak to walk**.* (negative) · *He is **strong enough to lift** it.* · *He was **so kind as to help** us.*",
"**only to** (unhappy result): *He ran to the station, **only to find** the train gone.*",
"**adjective + to-infinitive:** *easy to solve, sure to win, ready to go, glad to meet.* **Noun + to-infinitive:** *a house **to let**, time **to leave**, the first **to arrive**, nothing **to eat**, a chance **to win**.*",
"**wh-word + to:** *I don't know **what to do**. She told me **where to go**.* (*Why* never takes *to*.)",
"**It + be + adjective + (of/for) + to:** *It is kind **of** you to help. / It is easy **for** me to solve this.* (*of* = character; *for* = situation)",
"**Absolute infinitive phrases:** *to be honest, to tell the truth, to cut a long story short, to begin with, needless to say, so to speak.*",
"**Bare infinitive after:** *had better, would rather, would sooner, why not, cannot but, do nothing but, rather than, let's, help*: *You **had better go**. · He did nothing but **laugh**. · I cannot but **admire** him.*",
"**Be + to-infinitive** (plan, order, fate): *The Prime Minister **is to address** the nation. · He **was never to return**.*",
